  "configuration_id": "config_012",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (scvi_n200, singleprofile) achieves 52% accuracy vs. image (ViT-L) at only 22.7%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. However, we have only one RNA data point, so we cannot yet judge whether 52% reflects the ceiling of RNA-based models or is specific to the scvi_n200 encoder. Uncertainty: Whether the RNA encoder choice (learned scvi vs. linear PCA) materially affects performance. This experiment (config_012: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is a clean single-variable comparison to config_009, isolating the RNA encoder effect while holding profile setting and modality constant. It is the best use of the next budget slot because: (1) it reduces uncertainty about the RNA baseline before investing in more complex multimodal experiments, (2) if PCA matches or beats scvi_n200, it signals that the signal is linearly accessible and multimodal fusion may be more feasible; if PCA is much worse, it confirms the value of learned RNA representations and guides which encoder to pair with image in multimodal settings, (3) it changes only one variable, making the result interpretable."
}

